  "body": {
    "id": "lem:causal-identification",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Let \\(P\\) satisfy the observable clean-comparison equalities and admit \\(Q\\in\\mathcal M\\) that induces \\(P\\), with mean no anticipation imposed on every retained finite target or comparison cohort.  For every \\(k=(g,t)\\in\\mathcal K\\) and every \\(c\\in\\mathcal J_k\\),\n\\[\nq_{k,c}(X)=E_Q[Y_t(g,1)-Y_t(\\infty,1)\\mid G=g,S=1,X]\\qquad P_X\\text{-almost surely}.\n\\]\nConsequently\n\\[\n\\theta_k(P)=E_Q[Y_t(g,1)-Y_t(\\infty,1)\\mid G=g,S=1],\\qquad\n\\tau_\\omega(P)=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal K}\\omega_k\\theta_k(P),\n\\]\nand the centered ratio-functional OVS score is\n\\[\n\\Psi_{k,c,P}(O)=R_{k,c,P}(O)-\\frac{\\theta_k(P)}{\\pi_{g,1}}\\mathbf 1\\{G=g,S=1\\}.\n\\]",
    "free_symbols": [
      "Q",
      "P",
      "calM",
      "calK",
      "calJ",
      "q",
      "X",
      "Ypot",
      "G",
      "S",
      "theta",
      "tauomega",
      "omega",
      "Psi",
