    ],
    "justification": "This fixes the causal target before any efficiency calculation and retains the denominator derivative through \\(\\pi_{g,1}\\).",
    "gap": "Ortiz-Villavicencio and Sant'Anna (2025, Theorem 4.1) establish identification under their conditional-mean no-anticipation and period-by-period DDD parallel-trends conditions; this lemma records the exact reduction used here rather than claiming novelty.",
    "consumer": "Every later tangent, score, and package result targets the same prespecified aggregate rather than a data-adaptive estimand.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(k=(g,t)\\), \\(c\\in\\mathcal J_k\\), and \\(u\\in\\{g,\\ldots,t\\}\\).  Consistency gives\n\\[\nm_{g,1,u}(X)=E_Q[\\Delta Y_u(g,1)\\mid G=g,S=1,X].\n\\tag{C1}\n\\]\nNo effect on ineligible units and consistency give\n\\[\nm_{g,0,u}(X)=E_Q[\\Delta Y_u(\\infty,0)\\mid G=g,S=0,X],\n\\quad\nm_{c,0,u}(X)=E_Q[\\Delta Y_u(\\infty,0)\\mid G=c,S=0,X].\n\\tag{C2}\n\\]\nBecause \\(c>t\\ge u\\), mean no anticipation at \\(u\\) and \\(u-1\\), followed by consistency, gives\n\\[\nm_{c,1,u}(X)=E_Q[\\Delta Y_u(\\infty,1)\\mid G=c,S=1,X];\n\\tag{C3}\n\\]\nwhen \\(c=\\infty\\), (C3) is immediate.  Subtracting the conditional parallel-gap equality from (C1)--(C3) yields\n\\[\nm_{g,1,u}-m_{g,0,u}-m_{c,1,u}+m_{c,0,u}\n=E_Q[\\Delta Y_u(g,1)-\\Delta Y_u(\\infty,1)\\mid G=g,S=1,X].\n\\tag{C4}\n\\]\nSumming (C4) from \\(g\\) through \\(t\\) telescopes.  Mean no anticipation at \\(g-1<g\\) removes the lower endpoint, hence\n\\[\nq_{k,c}(X)=E_Q[Y_t(g,1)-Y_t(\\infty,1)\\mid G=g,S=1,X].\n\\tag{C5}\n\\]\nCell overlap implies \\(\\pi_{g,1}=E_P[p_{g,1}(X)]\\ge\\varepsilon>0\\).  Multiplying (C5) by \\(p_{g,1}(X)/\\pi_{g,1}\\), integrating over \\(P_X\\), and applying iterated expectation gives\n\\[\n\\theta_k(P)=\\frac{E_P[p_{g,1}(X)q_{k,c}(X)]}{\\pi_{g,1}}\n=E_Q[Y_t(g,1)-Y_t(\\infty,1)\\mid G=g,S=1].\n\\tag{C6}\n\\]\nThe aggregate formula follows from the definition of \\(\\tau_\\omega\\).  Finally every residual in Definition \\(\\ref{def:pairwise-score}\\) has conditional mean zero, so\n\\[\nE_P[\\Psi_{k,c,P}(O)\\mid X]\n=\\frac{p_{g,1}(X)}{\\pi_{g,1}}\\{q_{k,c}(X)-\\theta_k(P)\\}.\n\\tag{C7}\n\\]\nEquation (C7) is exactly the displayed denominator-corrected ratio score; it retains the derivative of \\(\\pi_{g,1}\\).",
